122:  - #335: the ×1 playback tap reads 21.000 or 86.333 ms early, by host session; the instruments trim it (SR-17). Answered by spec §11 #335: on a track holding a ×1 clip alone, the PostEffects tap stamps its samples one 4,096-frame buffer early (−85.333 ms, 3 runs). The PreEffects tap, which is the product `AudioTap`'s flag, reads +0.000 ms, as does the export. Preview audio is in sync, and no product code changed.
124:  - #337: a time-scaled clip's exported audio overruns or falls short of the timeline, run to run. CX2's `prores_422` audio was 196 095 frames in one run on a 4 s (192 000-frame) timeline, and CK05's was 1 213 frames (≈ 25 ms) short. U1 compares over the common length. Fixed by spec §11 #337: every export's audio is now exactly round(range × 48 000) frames, cut at the end and padded with silence (`ExportAudioEnd`; `retimed_audio_proof.py` A1–A3).
